           ------------------------
           Apache XMLSchema - Security
           ------------------------

Security and CVE Tracking

  This page tracks known vulnerabilities (CVEs) for Apache XMLSchema.

  For reporting a new vulnerability, see
  {{{https://www.apache.org/security/}Apache Security Team}}.

Apache XMLSchema CVEs

  * {{{https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2026-102495}CVE-2026-102495}}:
    Apache XMLSchema: Denial of service through unbounded recursion when
    resolving schema imports and includes

    * Severity: Low

    * Affected versions:

      - Apache XMLSchema before 2.3.3

    * Description:

      Apache XmlSchema doesn't limit how deeply schema imports and includes
      can be nested, so a malicious schema can make parsing recurse until the
      stack overflows. This causes a denial of service. Users are recommended
      to upgrade to version 2.3.3, which fixes this issue.

    * Credit:

      This issue was found using Claude agents to study the security of
      open-source projects (finder)

  * {{{https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2026-102496}CVE-2026-102496}}:
    Apache XMLSchema: Denial of service through deeply nested schema
    structures

    * Severity: Low

    * Affected versions:

      - Apache XMLSchema before 2.3.3

    * Description:

      Apache XmlSchema doesn't limit how deeply schema structures can be
      nested when it builds its schema model, so a malicious schema can make
      parsing recurse until the stack overflows. This causes a denial of
      service. Users are recommended to upgrade to version 2.3.3, which fixes
      this issue.

    * Credit:

      This issue was found using Claude agents to study the security of
      open-source projects (finder)

  * {{{https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2026-102497}CVE-2026-102497}}:
    Apache XMLSchema: Denial of service through cyclic schema definitions in
    the schema walker

    * Severity: Low

    * Affected versions:

      - Apache XMLSchema before 2.3.3

    * Description:

      The Apache XmlSchema walker (xmlschema-walker) doesn't detect cycles in
      type derivation, substitution groups, model groups or attribute groups.
      A malicious schema with such a cycle can make the walker recurse until
      the stack overflows, causing a denial of service. Users are recommended
      to upgrade to version 2.3.3, which fixes this issue.

    * Credit:

      This issue was found using Claude agents to study the security of
      open-source projects (finder)

